WEBVTT

00:01.710 --> 00:03.837
[theme music playing]

00:22.981 --> 00:24.858
DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON

01:35.470 --> 01:36.972
[groans]

01:38.223 --> 01:39.891
[Laios] <i>Something smells good.</i>

01:41.017 --> 01:42.978
[Chilchuck groans]

01:45.188 --> 01:46.356
Hey, Senshi?

01:46.439 --> 01:48.066
[Senshi grunting]

01:50.735 --> 01:52.404
[exclaims, chuckles]

01:52.487 --> 01:53.947
There you are.

01:54.030 --> 01:55.907
[Senshi] Oh, you're awake now.

01:55.991 --> 01:57.284
Good morning to you.

01:57.909 --> 01:59.452
I see you made breakfast.

01:59.536 --> 02:00.704
Isn't it great?

02:00.787 --> 02:02.706
Mr. Senshi is an amazing chef.

02:02.789 --> 02:04.416
-Yeah. You're right.
-[Senshi] Hmm.

02:04.499 --> 02:06.459
Senshi is the best there is.

02:06.543 --> 02:10.463
BREAKFAST PREPARED BY SENSHI

02:10.547 --> 02:12.716
[light music playing]

02:15.343 --> 02:17.721
Mmm. So tasty!

02:18.221 --> 02:19.139
-[Senshi] Yaad.
-Huh?

02:19.222 --> 02:20.849
Do you wanna try some too?

02:21.850 --> 02:24.019
[Yaad] But I won't be able to taste it.

02:24.102 --> 02:25.187
[Senshi] Here.

02:32.360 --> 02:33.361
[gulps]

02:33.445 --> 02:36.031
Oh, it's warm… and it's soft as well.

02:36.114 --> 02:39.075
[Senshi] Your sense of taste
is almost like a muscle.

02:39.159 --> 02:42.037
If you don't exercise it regularly,
then it gets weak.

02:42.120 --> 02:45.957
[Senshi] So start building it back up
by enjoying textures first.

02:46.041 --> 02:47.042
Got it.

02:47.125 --> 02:49.461
-Good. Stay still.
-[Izutsumi groaning]

02:50.420 --> 02:51.254
[Yaad sighs]

02:53.131 --> 02:54.758
A very long time ago,

02:54.841 --> 02:58.303
I used to dine with my parents
and grandfather like this.

02:58.386 --> 03:01.681
[Yaad]
<i>Always next to my grandfather was Thistle,</i>

03:01.765 --> 03:04.100
<i>who you may know as the mad mage.</i>

03:04.893 --> 03:06.895
-<i>My great-grandfather first brought him…</i>
-[young Thistle] Hold on!

03:06.978 --> 03:09.147
-<i>…to the castle as a court jester.</i>
-Come on, Thistle, hurry up!

03:09.230 --> 03:10.440
-<i>They say that the two of them…</i>
-[pants]

03:10.523 --> 03:12.317
-Wait for me!
-<i>…were raised like brothers.</i>

03:12.400 --> 03:15.195
<i>Once my grandfather ascended the throne,</i>

03:15.278 --> 03:18.823
<i>Thistle was asked to learn magic
and excelled in it.</i>

03:19.449 --> 03:23.328
<i>These lands were originally filled
with dwarven and elven artifacts,</i>

03:23.411 --> 03:26.331
<i>so there was likely
black magic mixed in too.</i>

03:27.040 --> 03:29.876
<i>Thistle soon became obsessed with power</i>

03:29.960 --> 03:33.213
<i>and eventually cast
a spell of immortality on us.</i>

03:33.922 --> 03:36.424
Actually, we've been wanting
to talk to him.

03:37.008 --> 03:38.593
Do you know where he is right now?

03:38.677 --> 03:40.136
Talk to him?

03:40.220 --> 03:42.389
You're asking for the impossible!

03:42.472 --> 03:44.849
A normal conversation
is out of the question.

03:44.933 --> 03:48.687
[Yaad] <i>We went through great trouble
to help my grandfather escape.</i>

03:48.770 --> 03:51.481
<i>Those suspected of helping were executed.</i>

03:52.565 --> 03:54.484
But if you just wanna meet him,

03:54.567 --> 03:59.197
the mage's eyes have started gathering
because they've noticed a change here.

03:59.281 --> 04:01.950
The mad mage himself
will appear before long.

04:03.243 --> 04:06.538
[Yaad] <i>This dungeon is
an extension of his arms and legs.</i>

04:07.163 --> 04:10.000
<i>You are aware of his power, aren't you?</i>

04:10.583 --> 04:12.460
We are, but we still need to see him.

04:13.878 --> 04:16.131
[Yaad]
I don't know if you'll be able to talk.

04:16.214 --> 04:18.466
<i>But go seek help from the Winged Lion</i>

04:18.550 --> 04:20.969
<i>that is imprisoned
deep within the dungeon.</i>

04:21.553 --> 04:24.389
<i>He might be able to subdue
the mage's power.</i>

04:24.973 --> 04:26.808
[birds chirping]

04:29.477 --> 04:31.980
[Yaad] You can get inside
the castle walls through here.

04:32.063 --> 04:34.774
Meaning, you'll be able
to return to the dungeon.

04:34.858 --> 04:36.901
Here you go. Take this with you.

04:36.985 --> 04:38.653
[Senshi] Thanks. You're too kind.

04:39.237 --> 04:40.864
Let's not give them too much.

04:40.947 --> 04:43.366
It'll be a huge burden
for those carrying them.

04:43.450 --> 04:44.659
What does that mean?

04:44.743 --> 04:48.371
Simply that you'll be leaving this place
the same way you came.

04:48.455 --> 04:50.415
-[eerie whooshing]
-[disgusted groan]

04:50.999 --> 04:52.876
[Laios] Thank you. All of you.

04:53.668 --> 04:54.753
[Yaad] Good luck.

04:57.172 --> 04:59.174
[Laios' party screaming]

05:00.550 --> 05:01.551
[sighs]

05:01.634 --> 05:03.011
I know I shouldn't say this,

05:03.094 --> 05:05.722
but do you really think
they're the chosen ones?

05:05.805 --> 05:07.807
I truly wish to think so.

05:09.976 --> 05:11.353
-[eerie sting]
-[Yaad gasps]

05:12.145 --> 05:13.271
Hey, Yaad.

05:13.355 --> 05:14.939
[exclaims]
Th… Thistle!

05:15.982 --> 05:16.900
[Thistle] Tell me.

05:16.983 --> 05:18.735
Who were you just talking to?

05:19.319 --> 05:22.238
[all screaming]

05:22.322 --> 05:23.656
-[all grunt]
-[loud thud]

05:24.699 --> 05:26.659
-[Marcille groans]
-Can we stop falling?

05:26.743 --> 05:27.869
Wait. This is…

05:27.952 --> 05:29.871
[Marcille] Ow, my back.

05:29.954 --> 05:32.457
[Laios] It's an ancient dwarven cistern.

05:32.540 --> 05:34.167
[Chilchuck] So it's this whole place, huh?

05:34.250 --> 05:35.752
Which part of it are we in?

05:36.503 --> 05:38.505
My compass isn't working.

05:38.588 --> 05:41.049
I guess I should've assumed
this would happen though.

05:41.132 --> 05:42.634
Typical dwarves.

05:42.717 --> 05:45.512
It looks like
the remains of a defensive point.

05:46.096 --> 05:47.055
[Laios] <i>Right?</i>

05:47.138 --> 05:48.515
[Senshi vomits]

05:48.598 --> 05:50.892
[Laios]
Oh, does he have traveling sickness?

05:50.975 --> 05:54.395
Probably, since dwarves have
sensitive semicircular canals.

05:54.479 --> 05:56.689
Is it the same for gnomes as well?

05:56.773 --> 05:59.275
[Marcille] That, on top of mana sickness,
I'd assume.

05:59.359 --> 06:00.276
[gasps]

06:00.360 --> 06:01.778
How do we get here?

06:01.861 --> 06:03.279
[Marcille] Oh, you're back?

06:03.363 --> 06:05.281
Huh? Wait. What…

06:05.365 --> 06:08.284
-[happy groaning in flashbacks]
-[shocked gasp, shriek]

06:08.368 --> 06:09.702
[Marcille] You okay?

06:09.786 --> 06:11.538
[Laios] Just rest here for a bit.

06:11.621 --> 06:13.289
-We're gonna take a look around.
-[whimpers]

06:13.373 --> 06:16.292
[wind howling]

06:16.876 --> 06:18.044
-[Senshi] Chil.
-Hmm?

06:18.128 --> 06:20.547
[Senshi]
You see these symbols on this pillar?

06:22.257 --> 06:24.926
Oh, yeah. I do see something.

06:25.009 --> 06:28.054
[Senshi] Write down the symbols
on the other pillars that are around us.

06:28.138 --> 06:30.557
I can tell roughly where we are that way.

06:30.640 --> 06:32.642
How do you know a thing like that?

06:32.725 --> 06:36.062
[Senshi] These types of places always have
some kind of hidden code in them.

06:36.771 --> 06:39.065
Well, I guess in this case,

06:39.149 --> 06:42.777
it just goes to show that not all dwarves
have a great sense of direction.

06:47.198 --> 06:48.575
I know where we are.

06:48.658 --> 06:50.743
Looks like we're somewhere
in the southeastern part--

06:50.827 --> 06:51.744
[Marcille] Hey!

06:51.828 --> 06:53.204
Guys, we found something!

06:53.288 --> 06:55.081
-[Chilchuck] Huh? That was fast.
-[Marcille panting]

06:55.790 --> 06:57.709
We might have found where Falin is!

06:58.334 --> 07:00.545
[Chilchuck]
You're saying these are Falin's tracks?

07:00.628 --> 07:03.339
[Marcille] She noticed us getting closer
and ran, but…

07:03.423 --> 07:04.924
it was definitely her.

07:05.008 --> 07:07.260
The silhouette said it all! Right?

07:07.343 --> 07:08.761
[Laios] Hmm…

07:08.845 --> 07:11.306
It seemed a lot closer to a griffin to me.

07:11.389 --> 07:12.223
[Senshi gasps]

07:12.307 --> 07:14.976
[Senshi] Re… Remind me what a griffin is.

07:15.059 --> 07:18.563
Its upper half is a bird,
and its lower half is a lion.

07:18.646 --> 07:21.566
There aren't records of this dungeon
ever having a griffin.

07:21.649 --> 07:22.484
[shivers]

07:23.067 --> 07:24.736
[Marcille] Is this scent familiar?

07:24.819 --> 07:26.654
[Chilchuck] We're not dogs, you know?

07:26.738 --> 07:27.739
[sniffs]

07:28.865 --> 07:29.908
[sniffs]

07:29.991 --> 07:31.493
It reeks of beast.

07:31.576 --> 07:33.620
Either way, we need to catch up to it.

07:33.703 --> 07:34.621
[Senshi] No, we don't.

07:35.497 --> 07:36.623
[Marcille] Huh?

07:36.706 --> 07:38.291
We don't? But why?

07:38.374 --> 07:40.293
[Senshi] Uh, well, it's just…

07:40.376 --> 07:41.878
It might be Falin, Senshi.

07:41.961 --> 07:43.254
[Senshi] I-- Um…

07:43.338 --> 07:44.464
Oh, over there!

07:44.547 --> 07:46.633
I've never seen
that kind of mushroom before.

07:46.716 --> 07:47.884
Let's cook it.

07:47.967 --> 07:49.010
Seriously?

07:49.093 --> 07:51.221
[Chilchuck]
They look vaguely familiar to me.

07:51.304 --> 07:53.348
That said,
I'm pretty sure they're poisonous,

07:53.431 --> 07:54.641
so don't eat them.

07:54.724 --> 07:56.809
[Senshi] I really don't like griffins.

07:56.893 --> 07:59.646
Why are you so scared of a monster
you've never even seen?

07:59.729 --> 08:00.855
Whatever. Let's just go!

08:00.939 --> 08:03.316
-[Senshi] No, please! Wait a minute!
-[grunts]

08:03.399 --> 08:04.817
-[Senshi] It's too dangerous out here!
-[gasps]

08:04.901 --> 08:06.194
Move!
[grunts]

08:06.277 --> 08:08.279
[suspenseful music playing]

08:10.406 --> 08:12.325
Whoa. I knew it…

08:12.408 --> 08:13.785
[Laios] The griffin!

08:15.411 --> 08:16.788
[griffin screeches]

08:16.871 --> 08:17.830
-[whooshes]
-[grunts]

08:18.456 --> 08:19.457
[Laios] How cool!

08:19.541 --> 08:21.292
It's my first time seeing one!

08:21.376 --> 08:22.752
[Marcille] A griffin?

08:23.419 --> 08:25.838
So I got all worked up for nothing?

08:27.298 --> 08:29.092
-Here it comes!
-Leave it to me!

08:29.175 --> 08:30.176
[Marcille] Now…

08:30.260 --> 08:32.095
<i>Spelae Yeptum Lufelms.</i>

08:32.178 --> 08:34.597
-[breathing heavily]
-[Marcille] <i>Lufelms Spelae Alamandras.</i>

08:34.681 --> 08:37.350
<i>Tronsum Yovis Stantinus Histum…</i>

08:37.433 --> 08:39.185
[Senshi screaming]

08:40.687 --> 08:42.063
[Marcille] Agh! It's too fast!

08:42.146 --> 08:44.732
[Laios] Senshi! Don't run away
with your back turned to it!

08:44.816 --> 08:47.235
[panicked panting]

08:48.861 --> 08:49.779
[gasps]

08:49.862 --> 08:52.865
[terrified screaming]

08:52.949 --> 08:54.909
[both] Senshi!
[grunt]

08:54.993 --> 08:57.537
[all panting]

08:59.581 --> 09:01.833
[panting continues]

09:03.001 --> 09:04.127
[Laios] Oh, no.

09:05.670 --> 09:08.047
It happened so fast. I was useless.

09:08.131 --> 09:10.300
[Marcille]
Did anyone see if he had a weapon on him?

09:10.383 --> 09:11.843
[Chilchuck] He didn't have one.

09:11.926 --> 09:13.219
[Laios] We have to go find him!

09:13.803 --> 09:16.514
Maybe someone should climb
on top of each pillar to look?

09:16.598 --> 09:18.099
Ain't gonna be me though.

09:18.182 --> 09:19.851
[Laios] <i>Which way did they go?</i>

09:19.934 --> 09:22.312
<i>We can't do anything
if they're somewhere up high.</i>

09:22.395 --> 09:24.105
<i>We won't even find his corpse.</i>

09:24.689 --> 09:26.608
<i>He has no way to defend himself.</i>

09:26.691 --> 09:29.027
<i>Are we really never gonna see him again?</i>

09:29.110 --> 09:31.738
Marcille, how do we save Senshi?

09:31.821 --> 09:32.655
[gasps]

09:33.197 --> 09:35.366
[groaning]

09:35.950 --> 09:38.119
I'll use a Familiar to find him.

09:38.202 --> 09:41.080
You're going to… summon a monster?

09:41.581 --> 09:44.792
It's not so much "summoning one"
as it is "creating one".

09:44.876 --> 09:46.628
There are three types of summoning.

09:46.711 --> 09:50.840
[Marcille] <i>One, taking control
of existing spirits or monsters.</i>

09:50.923 --> 09:52.759
<i>The conditions for it are complicated,</i>

09:52.842 --> 09:55.887
<i>and it's likely,
the lord of the dungeon will notice.</i>

09:55.970 --> 09:59.557
<i>Two, turning plants or animals
into monsters.</i>

09:59.641 --> 10:03.394
<i>This one also isn't ideal
because you need a lot of prep time.</i>

10:03.478 --> 10:04.395
[Marcille] Three.

10:04.479 --> 10:06.147
Making them yourself.

10:06.230 --> 10:07.565
That's what I'll be doing.

10:07.649 --> 10:09.651
[Laios]
That one sounds the most difficult.

10:09.734 --> 10:12.695
[Marcille] It is if you're trying to make
a fully independent creature.

10:12.779 --> 10:15.657
But for now, we just need it
to be able to move at least.

10:17.283 --> 10:19.327
While I prep the magic circle,

10:19.410 --> 10:21.704
can you gather
all the meat we have in the pan?

10:21.788 --> 10:22.789
[Laios] Sure thing.

10:22.872 --> 10:24.791
[upbeat tense music playing]

10:26.084 --> 10:27.126
[Laios] Hmm?

10:27.210 --> 10:28.336
That's everything?

10:28.419 --> 10:30.463
It'd be nice if you could find a bit more.

10:33.257 --> 10:34.425
There. That's it.

10:34.509 --> 10:36.302
Although, we do have some cheese and eggs.

10:36.386 --> 10:37.387
[Chilchuck] Veggies too!

10:37.470 --> 10:38.971
[Marcille] Hmm…

10:39.055 --> 10:41.474
Guess it'd still add to the calories.

10:41.557 --> 10:42.975
-Bring them.
-Right.

10:45.061 --> 10:47.271
[upbeat tribal music playing]

10:48.147 --> 10:49.774
What monster are you making?

10:49.857 --> 10:51.526
Is it gonna obey you?

10:51.609 --> 10:52.610
Could you teach me how to--

10:52.694 --> 10:53.528
No!

10:53.611 --> 10:57.115
Go and get yourself certified
to handle dangerous magic first!

10:57.699 --> 10:58.533
[sad groan]

10:58.616 --> 11:00.451
Wait. Is that really a thing?

11:00.535 --> 11:04.205
So, who exactly
is that old dwarf guy anyway?

11:04.288 --> 11:06.666
[Izutsumi] How'd he end up
in your party in the first place?

11:06.749 --> 11:09.168
And why is he so obsessed
with making food?

11:10.294 --> 11:11.212
[both] Hmm…

11:11.295 --> 11:12.130
Huh?

11:12.213 --> 11:13.923
How do you not know the answer to that?

11:14.006 --> 11:15.716
You all act like you're old buddies!

11:15.800 --> 11:18.761
I mean, I suppose
we've never had a chance to ask.

11:18.845 --> 11:22.223
I can relate not wanting
to discuss personal matters with people.

11:22.807 --> 11:23.975
Although…

11:24.058 --> 11:26.561
<i>I'd be lying if I said I wasn't curious.</i>

11:26.644 --> 11:29.480
<i>There are several things
that I'm still hung up on.</i>

11:30.064 --> 11:32.692
Do you remember what he said to us
back when we first met him?

11:33.234 --> 11:37.363
It's been a decade since he started
researching monster food in this dungeon.

11:37.447 --> 11:40.867
[Chilchuck] <i>But this dungeon
was only discovered six years ago.</i>

11:40.950 --> 11:42.243
[Laios] <i>That's true.</i>

11:42.326 --> 11:44.954
[Chilchuck] <i>Also,
every single piece of cookware he uses</i>

11:45.037 --> 11:46.956
<i>is made from high-quality metal.</i>

11:47.039 --> 11:49.709
<i>He was able to decipher
ancient dwarven codes.</i>

11:49.792 --> 11:52.753
<i>He's afraid of a monster
from a floor we just reached.</i>

11:52.837 --> 11:55.006
<i>And he always treats me like a child.</i>

11:55.089 --> 11:57.508
Isn't that last one a misunderstanding?

11:57.592 --> 11:58.468
[Chilchuck] No.

11:58.551 --> 12:01.888
People who don't know about our kind
usually jump to that conclusion.

12:01.971 --> 12:04.682
They don't realize
that half-foots are another race.

12:04.765 --> 12:08.394
So they assume that we become
a tall-man or a dwarf when we get older.

12:08.478 --> 12:12.815
However, that only comes
from a few regions, like the East.

12:12.899 --> 12:16.235
If he's lived here ten years,
there's no reason he shouldn't know.

12:16.319 --> 12:17.278
[gasps]

12:17.361 --> 12:20.490
Could it be
that Senshi… isn't from the surface?

12:21.532 --> 12:23.784
Sometime after we rescue him,

12:23.868 --> 12:26.704
why don't we ask him
to reintroduce himself to us?

12:28.039 --> 12:28.915
[Chilchuck groans]

12:28.998 --> 12:30.208
-[chimes]
-[Laios] Huh?

12:30.291 --> 12:33.377
[Marcille] <i>Spelae Yeptum Lufelms.</i>

12:33.461 --> 12:36.589
<i>Lufelms Spelae Viralu Indumreezbam.</i>

12:36.672 --> 12:39.300
-<i>Martis Tilnunto Eesdum.</i>
-[burbling]

12:39.383 --> 12:43.387
<i>Histum Elles Anjarkant Rementalento.</i>

12:43.471 --> 12:45.431
-[hissing]
-[Izutsumi] Whoa!

12:50.937 --> 12:52.230
Is it over now?

12:53.147 --> 12:54.232
It should be.

12:54.815 --> 12:56.859
Let's try to open the lid.

12:58.319 --> 12:59.946
[hissing]

13:00.029 --> 13:02.448
[tense music playing]

13:05.284 --> 13:07.203
[music intensifies]

13:07.286 --> 13:09.497
[hissing]

13:09.580 --> 13:11.582
[all chirping]

13:12.291 --> 13:14.210
[dramatic sting]

13:14.293 --> 13:16.337
Ah! Oh, thank goodness.

13:16.420 --> 13:18.756
I was almost worried I wouldn't succeed!

13:18.839 --> 13:21.676
[Marcille] What's that face?
I said they just needed to move, right?

13:21.759 --> 13:25.096
I couldn't spare the resources
to make them aesthetically pleasing, okay?

13:25.179 --> 13:27.431
-Now go!
-[chirping]

13:27.515 --> 13:28.933
[gasps, groans]

13:29.016 --> 13:30.560
What's wrong?

13:30.643 --> 13:33.271
[Marcille]
Its vision is overlapping with my own,

13:33.354 --> 13:34.689
and it feels awful.

13:34.772 --> 13:36.691
Can someone put a blindfold on me?

13:38.776 --> 13:41.445
How can the mad mage send out
so many of these things

13:41.529 --> 13:43.823
and also process their info all at once?

13:43.906 --> 13:44.949
I'm curious.

13:45.032 --> 13:46.784
You can think about that stuff later.

13:46.867 --> 13:48.077
Senshi first.

13:48.160 --> 13:49.537
I'll look for abnormalities

13:49.620 --> 13:52.665
based on the Dungeon Cleaners
and spirits around here.

13:52.748 --> 13:54.333
[Marcille] Follow my Familiar!

13:54.417 --> 13:56.294
[Marcille] Uh…

13:56.377 --> 13:57.295
[Laios] Huh?

13:57.378 --> 13:59.630
[Chilchuck]
Are you not gonna be able to keep up?

13:59.714 --> 14:02.216
[Marcille] Do you know
how hard it is to walk while flying?

14:02.300 --> 14:03.968
I'm gonna carry her.

14:04.051 --> 14:06.053
Would you two mind carrying our bags?

14:06.679 --> 14:08.931
-[Laios] And up we go.
-[Marcille whimpers]

14:09.015 --> 14:11.100
Wait! I'm scared!
[whimpers]

14:11.183 --> 14:12.852
-[Laios] Grab around here.
-[Marcille] No way!

14:12.935 --> 14:14.228
Are you trying to make me fall?

14:14.312 --> 14:15.479
-[Laios] Stop moving so much!
-[Marcille screams]

14:18.816 --> 14:20.484
The hell is she doing with her arms?

14:20.568 --> 14:23.237
-I guess this is what makes her feel safe.
-[Marcille panting]

14:26.240 --> 14:27.241
[Marcille gasps]

14:30.578 --> 14:31.495
[Marcille] That pillar!

14:31.579 --> 14:34.498
The Dungeon Cleaners are flocking to it!
That's the place!

14:37.043 --> 14:38.336
[Marcille] Senshi!

14:38.419 --> 14:39.712
There! Found him!

14:39.795 --> 14:41.756
The griffin trapped him
on a pillar up ahead!

14:41.839 --> 14:43.966
I see. Griffins do that?

14:44.050 --> 14:47.136
[Marcille] <i>We're here to save you, Senshi!
Can you tell it's me?</i>

14:47.219 --> 14:48.220
[Senshi] A fly?

14:48.304 --> 14:50.723
[grunting]

14:50.806 --> 14:51.891
[panting]

14:51.974 --> 14:54.352
[Marcille] <i>Crap. How do I get him down?</i>

14:54.435 --> 14:56.228
Just be careful, Marcille.

14:56.312 --> 14:58.356
Griffins have exceptional vision.

14:58.439 --> 15:00.733
[Laios] It'll already be watching you…

15:00.816 --> 15:02.360
before you even notice it.

15:02.443 --> 15:03.277
[Marcille gasps]

15:03.986 --> 15:04.820
[pained grunt]

15:04.904 --> 15:07.490
Ah… I lost my eyes up there.

15:08.616 --> 15:10.826
[Laios]
Griffins' bodies are very functional.

15:11.327 --> 15:12.662
Their wings are powerful,

15:12.745 --> 15:15.831
and their graceful bodies
allow them to adapt quickly.

15:15.915 --> 15:17.959
Plus, their sharp beak and claws,

15:18.042 --> 15:19.835
they're near impossible to avoid.

15:20.419 --> 15:23.089
[Laios] <i>Creatures are the way they look
because of necessity.</i>

15:23.172 --> 15:26.092
<i>They have no need
to just be aesthetically pleasing.</i>

15:26.175 --> 15:28.177
Hmm… Fine then.

15:28.260 --> 15:30.888
What shape should it take
to match up to a griffin?

15:32.056 --> 15:32.974
Hmm.

15:35.184 --> 15:37.436
Are you sure that horn is necessary?

15:37.520 --> 15:40.189
This shape will make it
a lot more aerodynamic.

15:40.272 --> 15:42.984
So now,
it'll be able to move much quicker.

15:43.651 --> 15:46.779
[Laios] <i>Do you remember the Wyverns
that the mad mage had patrolling?</i>

15:46.862 --> 15:48.948
<i>They were as fast as an arrow.</i>

15:49.031 --> 15:50.866
<i>Let's try to aim for that shape.</i>

15:50.950 --> 15:53.160
[uplifting music playing]

15:53.953 --> 15:56.872
[Laios] Send it out like this
and see the difference it makes.

15:57.623 --> 15:58.624
[grunts]

16:00.793 --> 16:04.005
It moves so fast now!
I think this will work!

16:04.088 --> 16:06.215
Until Senshi's back on the ground,

16:06.298 --> 16:08.300
I'll try to distract the griffin!

16:08.384 --> 16:10.594
Everyone else cover me
and prepare for battle!

16:10.678 --> 16:11.595
[panting]

16:11.679 --> 16:12.888
[Izutsumi] Why is she flapping?

16:12.972 --> 16:15.349
[Laios]
Maybe it gives her a sense of unity?

16:15.933 --> 16:17.351
[Marcille] <i>All right, Senshi.</i>

16:17.435 --> 16:19.311
<i>Grab on to this rope!</i>

16:19.937 --> 16:21.605
<i>Now, the next move is…</i>

16:21.689 --> 16:22.690
[Marcille gasps]

16:22.773 --> 16:23.733
<i>So fast!</i>

16:25.192 --> 16:26.736
<i>I have to lead it away!</i>

16:26.819 --> 16:28.738
<i>Come on, over here!</i>

16:30.072 --> 16:31.949
[suspenseful music playing]

16:33.034 --> 16:35.286
<i>Just get to the ground and…</i>

16:37.163 --> 16:38.789
-[music fades]
-[pained grunt]

16:41.250 --> 16:42.585
It got me again.

16:43.502 --> 16:44.503
This is bad.

16:44.587 --> 16:46.547
I can't even compete with it.

16:46.630 --> 16:47.548
What do I do?

16:47.631 --> 16:49.800
-[exciting music playing]
-You can leave everything to me!

16:49.884 --> 16:51.802
I've got this. I'll make it way stronger!

16:51.886 --> 16:54.472
[Laios] I'll put more horns here,
arrange the fangs,

16:54.555 --> 16:57.058
equip it with sharp claws,
add some scales, and…

16:57.141 --> 16:58.267
-give it two heads!
-[dragon screeches]

16:58.350 --> 17:00.603
Now all of its strength and abilities
are doubled!

17:00.686 --> 17:02.188
It breathes fire and ice!

17:02.271 --> 17:03.397
[Laios] So cool!
[cackling]

17:03.481 --> 17:05.983
[Marcille]
<i>How can it win a fight against a griffin?</i>

17:06.067 --> 17:08.694
<i>Does it need more attack or more defense?</i>

17:09.236 --> 17:10.071
<i>No!</i>

17:10.154 --> 17:12.156
[excited chuckle]
Huh?

17:12.948 --> 17:14.408
[Laios screaming]

17:14.492 --> 17:16.952
-My Giga Two-headed Flame Ice Dragon!
-<i>It doesn't need claws or fangs.</i>

17:17.036 --> 17:20.081
[Marcille] <i>Something fast,
elegant, and beautiful.</i>

17:20.581 --> 17:23.584
<i>What I need is the resolution and ego</i>

17:23.667 --> 17:26.962
<i>to create a creature
made solely to save Senshi!</i>

17:27.546 --> 17:31.050
[narrator] <i>It was in that moment
that all of Marcille's thoughts</i>

17:31.133 --> 17:32.343
<i>and her prayers</i>

17:32.426 --> 17:34.804
<i>manifested into a miracle.</i>

17:35.596 --> 17:37.348
I shall bestow you with a name.

17:37.431 --> 17:39.975
Silver wings that will soar the heavens!

17:40.059 --> 17:41.227
[chimes]

17:41.310 --> 17:44.355
[Marcille] I summon thee, Sky Fish!

17:44.438 --> 17:45.356
So…

17:46.148 --> 17:47.274
stupid.

17:47.358 --> 17:48.442
Shut up! It's fine!

17:49.026 --> 17:50.694
Now then, time to fly!

17:55.449 --> 17:57.743
[zapping]

17:57.827 --> 17:59.870
-So fast!
-It moves so creepily!

17:59.954 --> 18:01.330
I'm going all out!

18:01.413 --> 18:02.998
Everyone, prepare for battle!

18:03.082 --> 18:05.501
[Izutsumi] What the hell is she doing now?

18:05.584 --> 18:08.003
[Laios] Her best, or… something close.

18:10.381 --> 18:11.632
-[growls]
-[scared shriek]

18:11.715 --> 18:13.843
[Marcille shouting]

18:14.718 --> 18:15.678
[grunts]

18:15.761 --> 18:18.180
[Marcille]
<i>Whoa! It's hard to control this thing!</i>

18:18.264 --> 18:19.932
[epic music playing]

18:21.433 --> 18:23.936
<i>All right. Now this time…</i>

18:24.478 --> 18:26.522
<i>I'll turn around and…</i>

18:27.356 --> 18:28.649
<i>pierce through!</i>

18:28.732 --> 18:30.359
[screeches]

18:31.443 --> 18:32.278
[Laios grunts]

18:42.246 --> 18:43.289
[grunts]

18:44.081 --> 18:45.749
-[music fades]
-[groans]

18:50.880 --> 18:52.506
-[rope rustles]
-[Senshi grunts]

18:53.090 --> 18:54.216
[Chilchuck] Are you hurt?

18:54.300 --> 18:55.676
[Senshi] I'm fine.

18:55.759 --> 18:57.761
[Laios]
We should probably take a good rest.

18:57.845 --> 19:00.681
You go relax over there, Senshi,
while I do the cooking.

19:00.764 --> 19:01.765
[Marcille] Huh?

19:02.474 --> 19:03.642
[Marcille gasps]

19:09.857 --> 19:10.941
[Marcille] Thank you.

19:12.276 --> 19:13.485
Rest in peace.

19:14.486 --> 19:15.821
[Marcille] <i>My Sky Fish…</i>

19:18.240 --> 19:19.533
Whoa.

19:19.617 --> 19:21.410
This is actually pretty cool.

19:21.493 --> 19:23.996
[Laios] Vegetables are packed in there,
like organs.

19:25.247 --> 19:26.457
-[screams]
-[grunts]

19:26.540 --> 19:28.417
-Did… did you need it for something?
-[sobbing]

19:28.500 --> 19:30.211
No, not really, but…

19:31.003 --> 19:33.047
[Marcille] I just… you know,
I was hoping to have

19:33.130 --> 19:34.715
a little more time to mourn,

19:34.798 --> 19:35.966
and now I can't…

19:36.050 --> 19:37.968
Are you okay, Senshi?

19:38.052 --> 19:39.845
-[Senshi] Hmm…
-[Laios] And besides, eating its flesh

19:39.929 --> 19:42.056
can be considered
another way of mourning it.

19:42.139 --> 19:45.351
[Marcille] Yeah. I know, but…
[sobs]

19:46.602 --> 19:49.021
It's fine. Do whatever.

19:49.813 --> 19:52.775
[Laios] <i>Chop up the summoned creature
into the desired length.</i>

19:53.359 --> 19:54.944
<i>Trim off the wings at the base.</i>

19:55.611 --> 19:59.281
<i>Squeeze out all the moisture
with a scrap of cloth.</i>

19:59.365 --> 20:00.783
<i>Salt and pepper.</i>

20:00.866 --> 20:03.077
<i>Take the wings and roll them.</i>

20:03.661 --> 20:05.704
<i>Dunk each piece of meat
you chopped earlier</i>

20:05.788 --> 20:08.207
<i>into a mixture of flour, egg, and water.</i>

20:08.290 --> 20:10.459
-<i>Then fry.</i>
-[sizzling]

20:10.542 --> 20:13.837
<i>For the wings,
quickly dip them in oil to cook them.</i>

20:13.921 --> 20:16.090
<i>Serve with a sauce and…</i>

20:16.173 --> 20:17.258
it's ready!

20:17.341 --> 20:20.094
SKY FISH AND CHIPS

20:25.933 --> 20:29.270
This is seriously the perfect fusion
of meat and veggies.

20:29.353 --> 20:30.729
If you say so.

20:30.813 --> 20:34.441
You think summoning spells could play
a big part in the art of cooking?

20:34.525 --> 20:35.526
I sure hope not,

20:35.609 --> 20:38.988
considering you need to sacrifice
a week's worth of ingredients.

20:39.071 --> 20:42.241
Dammit. I knew I should've brought
some of that ale with me.

20:42.324 --> 20:45.160
[Marcille] Make sure you eat
more than just the wings, Izutsumi.

20:45.244 --> 20:46.203
Nuh-uh.

20:47.079 --> 20:48.622
Have a bite, Senshi.

20:48.706 --> 20:51.125
[Laios] Uh… worried about the griffin?

20:51.709 --> 20:54.628
-Would draining its blood help… maybe?
-[gasps]

20:54.712 --> 20:57.131
[Senshi] N-No. That's not it.

20:57.214 --> 21:00.050
I-I'm just not all that hungry
at the moment.

21:00.968 --> 21:02.344
[clears throat]

21:02.970 --> 21:04.638
Hey, uh, Senshi…

21:06.724 --> 21:09.101
My name is Chilchuck.

21:09.184 --> 21:13.063
I was born in a small village
found in a basin to the northeast.

21:14.398 --> 21:15.899
Since about ten years ago,

21:15.983 --> 21:18.694
I've been doing odd jobs
in various dungeons.

21:18.777 --> 21:22.114
Picklocking, translation,
even being the middleman.

21:22.990 --> 21:25.492
Also, I have a wife and kids,

21:25.576 --> 21:27.911
but for reasons,
I haven't seen them in a while.

21:27.995 --> 21:28.912
[shocked gasp]

21:29.496 --> 21:31.123
-A wife and kids?
-Well, that about sums it up

21:31.206 --> 21:32.374
for my backstory.

21:33.000 --> 21:35.419
You mind telling us some stuff about you?

21:36.003 --> 21:38.130
[Chilchuck]
How'd you end up living in this dungeon?

21:38.672 --> 21:39.965
Did something happen?

21:40.507 --> 21:42.509
[pensive music playing]

21:42.593 --> 21:43.510
[sighs]

21:45.888 --> 21:48.640
[Senshi] My name is Senshi of Izganda.

21:49.767 --> 21:52.436
I used to be
a member of a small mining group.

21:53.645 --> 21:55.647
[Senshi] <i>And while I say a mining group,</i>

21:55.731 --> 21:57.858
<i>we weren't actually looking
to collect ore.</i>

21:58.442 --> 22:01.695
<i>What we were really after
were ruins that stood before the war,</i>

22:01.779 --> 22:03.530
<i>hoping to strike it rich.</i>

22:04.114 --> 22:07.534
<i>But ore is most of what we dug up
each day, of course.</i>

22:07.618 --> 22:11.705
<i>If we were lucky, we would come across
a few relics like cogwheels and lenses</i>

22:11.789 --> 22:13.457
<i>every once in a while.</i>

22:14.083 --> 22:16.585
<i>Then one day, after some usual digging,</i>

22:17.127 --> 22:19.213
<i>we dug our way to something huge.</i>

22:19.838 --> 22:21.215
[amazed gasp]

22:22.132 --> 22:25.636
<i>An ancient castle
brilliantly shining with gold.</i>

22:26.303 --> 22:27.721
[Senshi] That's right.

22:27.805 --> 22:29.848
It was this very dungeon.

22:31.058 --> 22:33.060
[closing theme music playing]
